  "captions": [
   {
    "t": 0,
    "text": "4 August 1914. Germany's armies march west. The Schlieffen Plan sends a huge right wing through Belgium to sweep round Paris, while the left holds in Lorraine."
   },
   {
    "t": 2,
    "text": "The forts of Liège hold out for twelve days, until huge German and Austrian siege howitzers smash them. The Belgian army falls back to Antwerp."
   },
   {
    "t": 14,
    "text": "The French attack too, as their Plan XVII demands: into Lorraine and the Ardennes. Machine guns and artillery cut them down. On 22 August alone about 27,000 French soldiers are killed."
   },
   {
    "t": 19,
    "text": "23 August: the British fight at Mons, then retreat beside the French Fifth Army. For two weeks the Allies fall back towards Paris."
   },
   {
    "t": 27,
    "text": "German armies close on Paris. But to keep touch with its neighbour, Kluck's First Army swings east of the city instead of round it."
   },
   {
    "t": 33,
    "text": "6 September. Joffre strikes. The new French Sixth Army hits Kluck's flank on the Ourcq. The British and the French Fifth Army push into a gap opening between the German armies."
   },
   {
    "t": 36,
    "text": "9 September. Fearing a breakthrough, the Germans order a retreat. They dig in on the heights above the Aisne, and the Allies cannot shift them."
   },
   {
    "t": 44,
    "text": "Now each side tries to get round the other's northern flank. Armies are moved north by rail, and the race to the sea leapfrogs through Picardy and Artois."
   },
   {
    "t": 62,
    "text": "Antwerp falls on 10 October. The Belgian army escapes along the coast to the Yser. The British move north to Flanders."
   },
   {
    "t": 76,
    "text": "From 19 October Germany throws its last fresh corps at Ypres. The Belgians open the sluices and flood the Yser plain. The line holds."
   },
   {
    "t": 94,
    "text": "By November a line of trenches runs some 700 kilometres from the North Sea to Switzerland. It will barely move for three and a half years."
   }
  ]
 },
